  ARRAY_CONSTRUCT($$Live vehicle routing and repositioning solved with the VROOM optimizer running on Snowpark Container Services$$, $$A dedicated semantic view (SV_ASSET_VELOCITY) so the agent ranks idle assets and cost without new SQL$$, $$Cost model held in configuration rather than in someone's spreadsheet$$),
  ARRAY_CONSTRUCT($$Asset master with home base and class$$, $$Position or last-known-location history, to derive idle time$$, $$A daily holding or opportunity cost per asset class$$, $$Optional: forward demand or lane requirements to reposition against$$),
  ARRAY_CONSTRUCT($$Turn parked assets back into earning assets$$, $$Raise utilization enough to defer capital spend on more units$$, $$Give dispatch a defensible next move for every idle asset$$),
  $$Idle time is the gap since the asset last moved, filtered by the idle-days threshold set on screen. Cost of idleness is idle days multiplied by the configured daily cost for that class. The repositioning move is solved live against the road network and its rationale is generated on screen.$$,
  $$Synthetic assets and positions. Projected savings assume the repositioned asset actually finds work at the destination, so treat the figure as an upper bound.$$,
  $$query_asset_velocity$$,
  ARRAY_CONSTRUCT($$idle vehicle count$$, $$total cost of idleness (USD)$$, $$projected savings (USD)$$, $$average idle days$$, $$lane demand$$),
  ARRAY_CONSTRUCT($$Which vehicle has the highest cost of idleness?$$, $$What is the total cost of idleness?$$, $$Which dispatcher has the most idle vehicles?$$, $$How many CRITICAL-severity vehicles are there?$$),
  $$Asset Velocity (Asset Pool domain, view id: asset_velocity).
Headline: Find idle Vehicles, price what the idleness is costing, and get a live repositioning suggestion for each one.
Business question: Which of our Vehicles are sitting still, what is that costing us, and where should they go next?
Audience: Fleet asset manager; Dispatch manager; CFO; Yard and depot operations.
Industries: Road freight; Trailer and container leasing; Rail and intermodal; Equipment rental.
Talk track: Set the minimum idle-days threshold, then read the KPI row: idle count, cost of idleness, projected savings and average idle days.; Show the severity chart and focus on CRITICAL.; Click an idle Vehicle to highlight where it is parked.; Read the repositioning rationale, and note that the move is solved live against the road network rather than looked up in a table.; Convert the cost of idleness into the annual figure, which is the CFO's version of this story..
Snowflake capabilities: Live vehicle routing and repositioning solved with the VROOM optimizer running on Snowpark Container Services; A dedicated semantic view (SV_ASSET_VELOCITY) so the agent ranks idle assets and cost without new SQL; Cost model held in configuration rather than in someone's spreadsheet.
Data required: Asset master with home base and class; Position or last-known-location history, to derive idle time; A daily holding or opportunity cost per asset class; Optional: forward demand or lane requirements to reposition against.
Value drivers: Turn parked assets back into earning assets; Raise utilization enough to defer capital spend on more units; Give dispatch a defensible next move for every idle asset.
Method: Idle time is the gap since the asset last moved, filtered by the idle-days threshold set on screen. Cost of idleness is idle days multiplied by the configured daily cost for that class. The repositioning move is solved live against the road network and its rationale is generated on screen.
Caveats: Synthetic assets and positions. Projected savings assume the repositioned asset actually finds work at the destination, so treat the figure as an upper bound.
Key metrics on screen: idle vehicle count; total cost of idleness (USD); projected savings (USD); average idle days; lane demand.
Example questions: Which vehicle has the highest cost of idleness? What is the total cost of idleness? Which dispatcher has the most idle vehicles? How many CRITICAL-severity vehicles are there?
Gotchas: query_asset_velocity (SV_ASSET_VELOCITY) is the dedicated tool for idle vehicles, cost of idleness, projected savings, and lane demand; use it for ranking and breakdown questions. The four headline KPIs are published as on-screen metric values. idle_min is the active idle-day threshold and selected_vehicle is the clicked row. The AI repositioning rationale is generated on screen and is not in panel context.
Preferred analytics tool: query_asset_velocity.$$
