SELECT
  $$dwell_overview$$, $$Dwell Overview$$, $$Core$$,
  $$Fleet dwell-time analytics and SLA monitoring (scoped to the active region and vehicle).$$,
  $$How much of the day the fleet spends standing still, how that is trending, and how often it breaches the dwell SLA.$$,
  $$How much paid time are we losing to standing still, and are we meeting our turnaround commitments?$$,
  ARRAY_CONSTRUCT($$Operations manager$$, $$Supply chain lead$$, $$Site or yard manager$$, $$Carrier performance manager$$),
  ARRAY_CONSTRUCT($$Logistics and transport$$, $$Manufacturing inbound$$, $$Retail distribution$$, $$Ports and terminals$$),
  ARRAY_CONSTRUCT($$Read the four headline numbers: dwell sessions, average dwell minutes, SLA compliance rate and active Drivers.$$, $$Show the trend chart and say plainly whether dwell is getting better or worse.$$, $$Use the facilities chart to name the worst offenders.$$, $$Frame the cost: dwell is paid time with no movement attached to it.$$, $$Hand off to Facility Utilization for the site view, and to SLA Alerts for the breach queue.$$),
  ARRAY_CONSTRUCT($$Sessionization of raw pings into dwell events using Dynamic Tables that refresh incrementally$$, $$SLA thresholds held in configuration (DIM_VEHICLE_DWELL_SLA) rather than hardcoded in a report$$, $$One semantic view (SV_DWELL_ANALYTICS) answering both the dashboard and the agent$$),
  ARRAY_CONSTRUCT($$Position pings with timestamp$$, $$Site or facility master with location and detection radius$$, $$A dwell SLA threshold per vehicle class or site type$$),
  ARRAY_CONSTRUCT($$Recover paid hours lost at the dock or the kerb$$, $$Hold sites and carriers to a measured turnaround commitment$$, $$Free capacity without buying more Vehicles$$),
  $$Dwell sessions are sessionized from position pings: consecutive stationary pings inside a site radius are grouped into one session. SLA compliance is the fraction of sessions at or under the configured threshold, 30 minutes by default.$$,
  $$Synthetic telemetry. A stop shorter than the detection threshold is not a session at all, so very brief stops are invisible by design. This view has no map; use SLA Alerts for dwell geography.$$,
  $$query_dwell$$,
  ARRAY_CONSTRUCT($$total dwell sessions$$, $$average dwell minutes$$, $$SLA compliance rate$$, $$active drivers$$),
  ARRAY_CONSTRUCT($$What is the average dwell time?$$, $$What is the SLA compliance rate?$$, $$Which facility has the most visits?$$, $$Are dwells trending up or down?$$),
  $$Dwell Overview (Core domain, view id: dwell_overview).
Headline: How much of the day the fleet spends standing still, how that is trending, and how often it breaches the dwell SLA.
Business question: How much paid time are we losing to standing still, and are we meeting our turnaround commitments?
Audience: Operations manager; Supply chain lead; Site or yard manager; Carrier performance manager.
Industries: Logistics and transport; Manufacturing inbound; Retail distribution; Ports and terminals.
Talk track: Read the four headline numbers: dwell sessions, average dwell minutes, SLA compliance rate and active Drivers.; Show the trend chart and say plainly whether dwell is getting better or worse.; Use the facilities chart to name the worst offenders.; Frame the cost: dwell is paid time with no movement attached to it.; Hand off to Facility Utilization for the site view, and to SLA Alerts for the breach queue..
Snowflake capabilities: Sessionization of raw pings into dwell events using Dynamic Tables that refresh incrementally; SLA thresholds held in configuration (DIM_VEHICLE_DWELL_SLA) rather than hardcoded in a report; One semantic view (SV_DWELL_ANALYTICS) answering both the dashboard and the agent.
Data required: Position pings with timestamp; Site or facility master with location and detection radius; A dwell SLA threshold per vehicle class or site type.
Value drivers: Recover paid hours lost at the dock or the kerb; Hold sites and carriers to a measured turnaround commitment; Free capacity without buying more Vehicles.
Method: Dwell sessions are sessionized from position pings: consecutive stationary pings inside a site radius are grouped into one session. SLA compliance is the fraction of sessions at or under the configured threshold, 30 minutes by default.
Caveats: Synthetic telemetry. A stop shorter than the detection threshold is not a session at all, so very brief stops are invisible by design. This view has no map; use SLA Alerts for dwell geography.
Key metrics on screen: total dwell sessions; average dwell minutes; SLA compliance rate; active drivers.
Example questions: What is the average dwell time? What is the SLA compliance rate? Which facility has the most visits? Are dwells trending up or down?
Gotchas: SLA compliance is the fraction of dwell sessions at or under the 30-minute threshold. The four headline KPIs are published as on-screen metric values. query_dwell (SV_DWELL_ANALYTICS) can answer the 30-day daily trend and top-facility questions. This view has no map; for dwell hotspots on a map, use the SLA Alerts view.
Preferred analytics tool: query_dwell.$$
