Talk track: Open on the KPI row: active Vehicles, movement utilization, empty miles percentage and average speed for the current region and date scope.; Call out empty miles percentage as the money metric - it is the share of distance driven with no load.; Click a row in the Vehicle list to select one and show the map recentering on it.; Read the detail panel for that Vehicle: current state, last ping and recent movement.; Ask the assistant on the left how many Vehicles are moving right now, and show it answering from the same numbers that are on screen..
Snowflake capabilities: Fleet-scale GPS telemetry queried directly in Snowflake, with no extract and no separate geospatial database; Native GEOGRAPHY types and H3 spatial functions driving the map straight from SQL; One semantic view (SV_FLEET_OPS) serving both the dashboard and the Cortex agent, so the screen and the chat cannot disagree.
Data required: Vehicle or asset master (id, type, home base); Position pings with timestamp and location; Optional: trip or job records, to attribute loaded versus empty distance.
Value drivers: Cut empty running, which is cost with no revenue attached; Replace a morning roll-call spreadsheet with a live shared picture; Give dispatch one screen instead of one portal per telematics vendor.
Method: Positions are raw GPS pings. Utilization is the share of pings in a MOVING state, so it is a movement measure rather than a duty-cycle or paid-hours measure. Empty miles come from leg classification (laden versus empty), not from an assumption.
Caveats: The telemetry is synthetic, generated for the active region and vehicle type. Because utilization is ping-based, do not quote it as a contractual utilization figure.
Key metrics on screen: active Vehicles; movement utilization %; empty miles %; average speed.
Example questions: How many Vehicles are moving right now? What is our empty miles percentage? Which Vehicles are moving, idle, or on site at this moment? Where do we start if we want to reduce empty miles?
Gotchas: Positions are GPS pings; utilization is the share of pings in a MOVING state, not a duty-cycle measure.
Preferred analytics tool: query_fleet_ops.$$
