  $$How to point these dashboards and the assistant at a customer's real SAP plus telematics data without rebuilding anything above the contract.$$,
  $$Our asset master lives in SAP and our positions come from a telematics vendor. What does it take to run all of this on our own data?$$,
  ARRAY_CONSTRUCT($$Enterprise architect$$, $$Data platform lead$$, $$SAP data owner$$, $$Solution Engineer$$),
  ARRAY_CONSTRUCT($$Manufacturing$$, $$Utilities$$, $$Mining and heavy equipment$$, $$Transport and logistics$$),
  ARRAY_CONSTRUCT($$Frame the seam: the dashboards read a neutral contract, so binding customer data is a mapping exercise rather than an app rebuild.$$, $$Ask the assistant which SAP tables can be bound - it introspects the database live and lists what it finds.$$, $$Walk the join strategy question: how SAP equipment is matched to telematics devices, and why the crosswalk is mandatory.$$, $$Show that CDC-landed tables are deduped to current rows before they are bound.$$, $$Close on the payoff: the semantic view, every dashboard and the agent move across together, with no edits above the contract.$$),
  ARRAY_CONSTRUCT($$A neutral data contract that lets physical sources swap without touching dashboards, semantic views or the agent$$, $$Live introspection of a customer database through an audited agent tool$$, $$Cortex Search over the binding playbook, so guidance is retrieved rather than remembered$$),
  ARRAY_CONSTRUCT($$SAP EAM, SD and TM tables already landed in Snowflake (Fivetran, SLT, Datasphere or equivalent)$$, $$Telematics positions landed in the same account$$, $$A crosswalk that reliably matches an SAP asset to a telematics device$$),
  ARRAY_CONSTRUCT($$Get from demo to the customer's own data in days, using a documented mapping$$, $$Avoid a bespoke integration project per dashboard$$, $$Keep SAP as the system of record while the analytics run in Snowflake$$),
  $$This is a guidance page rather than analytics over fleet data. The assistant answers from a Cortex Search knowledge base of the binding playbook, and can introspect a target database live to list bindable objects.$$,
  $$SAP and telematics must be co-located in one Snowflake account before binding, and the asset crosswalk is mandatory - without a reliable asset-to-device match, nothing above the contract can be trusted. Maintenance objects and SAP write-back are later phases.$$,
  $$search_sap_binding$$,
  ARRAY_CONSTRUCT(),
  ARRAY_CONSTRUCT($$How do I match my SAP equipment to telematics devices?$$, $$What are the steps to bind my SAP data into the fleet dashboards?$$, $$Which join strategy should I use if SAP has no EQUI?$$, $$Which SAP tables can I bind in MOCK_SAP?$$),
  $$SAP Binding (Help domain, view id: sap_binding).
Headline: How to point these dashboards and the assistant at a customer's real SAP plus telematics data without rebuilding anything above the contract.
Business question: Our asset master lives in SAP and our positions come from a telematics vendor. What does it take to run all of this on our own data?
Audience: Enterprise architect; Data platform lead; SAP data owner; Solution Engineer.
Industries: Manufacturing; Utilities; Mining and heavy equipment; Transport and logistics.
Talk track: Frame the seam: the dashboards read a neutral contract, so binding customer data is a mapping exercise rather than an app rebuild.; Ask the assistant which SAP tables can be bound - it introspects the database live and lists what it finds.; Walk the join strategy question: how SAP equipment is matched to telematics devices, and why the crosswalk is mandatory.; Show that CDC-landed tables are deduped to current rows before they are bound.; Close on the payoff: the semantic view, every dashboard and the agent move across together, with no edits above the contract..
Snowflake capabilities: A neutral data contract that lets physical sources swap without touching dashboards, semantic views or the agent; Live introspection of a customer database through an audited agent tool; Cortex Search over the binding playbook, so guidance is retrieved rather than remembered.
Data required: SAP EAM, SD and TM tables already landed in Snowflake (Fivetran, SLT, Datasphere or equivalent); Telematics positions landed in the same account; A crosswalk that reliably matches an SAP asset to a telematics device.
Value drivers: Get from demo to the customer's own data in days, using a documented mapping; Avoid a bespoke integration project per dashboard; Keep SAP as the system of record while the analytics run in Snowflake.
Method: This is a guidance page rather than analytics over fleet data. The assistant answers from a Cortex Search knowledge base of the binding playbook, and can introspect a target database live to list bindable objects.
Caveats: SAP and telematics must be co-located in one Snowflake account before binding, and the asset crosswalk is mandatory - without a reliable asset-to-device match, nothing above the contract can be trusted. Maintenance objects and SAP write-back are later phases.
Example questions: How do I match my SAP equipment to telematics devices? What are the steps to bind my SAP data into the fleet dashboards? Which join strategy should I use if SAP has no EQUI? Which SAP tables can I bind in MOCK_SAP?
Gotchas: This is conceptual how-to knowledge, not analytics over fleet data. SAP and telematics must be co-located into one account first, and the ASSET_CROSSWALK is mandatory.
Preferred analytics tool: search_sap_binding.$$
