  $$sourcing_optimizer$$, $$Freight Sourcing Optimizer$$, $$Location$$,
  $$Plant-to-customer location swaps: for each customer, compare the live road-distance freight cost from the current source plant against the cheapest product-capable plant, and quantify the annual saving. Freight cost is driven by your per-km and per-ton-km rate inputs.$$,
  $$Serve each customer from the cheapest plant that can actually make their product, priced on real road distance.$$,
  $$Where are we shipping from the wrong plant, and what would re-sourcing save us in a year?$$,
  ARRAY_CONSTRUCT($$Supply chain director$$, $$Logistics and freight manager$$, $$CFO$$, $$Commercial operations$$),
  ARRAY_CONSTRUCT($$Building materials$$, $$Glass and packaging$$, $$Chemicals$$, $$Food and beverage manufacturing$$),
  ARRAY_CONSTRUCT($$Read the header: current annual freight spend, optimized spend and the total saving.$$, $$Show the swaps table sorted by saving and open the biggest one.$$, $$Put it on the map: current source plant versus proposed plant for that customer.$$, $$Move the per-km and per-ton-km sliders to the customer's real rates and watch the saving move.$$, $$Stress that the distance matrix is one live routing call over the road network, not straight lines.$$),
  ARRAY_CONSTRUCT($$A single live ORS MATRIX_TABULAR call producing an all-plants by all-customers road-distance matrix at interaction time$$, $$A table function that turns that matrix into rows and picks the winning source per customer in SQL$$, $$Product capability constraints enforced in the same query as the cost model$$),
  ARRAY_CONSTRUCT($$Plant locations with product capability$$, $$Customer locations with product and annual volume$$, $$Freight rates per km and per ton-km$$, $$A provisioned routing region containing all plants and customers$$),
  ARRAY_CONSTRUCT($$Cut freight spend with no capital investment - it is a sourcing decision, not a build$$, $$Quantify a re-sourcing business case customer by customer$$, $$Expose where straight-line planning has been quietly wrong$$),
  $$The plant-to-customer road-distance matrix is computed live with a single ORS MATRIX_TABULAR call (all plants by all customers), not precomputed. Freight cost per truckload = distance_km x rate per km + tons x distance_km x rate per ton-km. The current source is a data-only baseline (the nearest product-capable plant by straight-line distance); the optimizer picks the cheapest source by actual road distance, so the gap is the achievable saving. Only plants that can make the customer's product are considered, and annual savings are the per-load saving multiplied by the customer's annual truckloads.$$,
